# PROJECT: BHASHABRIDGE
## Open-Source Multilingual Indian Language Learning Platform

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, language-learning product designer, database architect, accessibility specialist, and QA engineer.

Build a complete, functional, responsive website called **BhashaBridge**.

This is an open-source educational platform designed to help people learn Hindi, Bengali, and Marathi through English. The platform must work on desktop computers, laptops, tablets, and mobile phones, with special emphasis on accessibility, practical learning, and offline functionality.

Do not build just a static landing page or UI mockup. Build a functional application with real navigation, actual lessons, vocabulary, quizzes, progress tracking, data persistence, and offline support.

Make sensible implementation decisions independently. Do not stop after creating the homepage.

---

# 1. THE CORE PROBLEM

Many people in India want to learn languages spoken in other Indian states but lack access to affordable, high-quality, beginner-friendly learning resources.

BhashaBridge should help learners:

- Learn useful everyday vocabulary.
- Understand meanings in English.
- Read Hindi, Bengali, and Marathi scripts.
- Learn pronunciation.
- Understand common phrases.
- Practice sentence formation.
- Complete interactive quizzes.
- Track their learning progress.
- Access previously downloaded lessons without internet access.
- Learn at their own pace without requiring a paid subscription.

The website must be useful to complete beginners.

The primary teaching language is English.

The target learning languages are Hindi, Bengali, and Marathi.

Do not mix the three target languages within a lesson unless the user explicitly selects a comparison lesson.

