# 5. WIKIMEDIA DATA INTEGRATION

The application must use Wikimedia resources responsibly.

Use the following approach.

## A. Wiktionary for vocabulary

Wiktionary is the preferred Wikimedia source for dictionary entries.

Use suitable Wikimedia APIs to retrieve word information when available.

Investigate:
- The MediaWiki Action API.
- Wiktionary entries.
- Definitions and translations.
- Available pronunciation information.
- Available audio files.
- Relevant language metadata.

Use documented endpoints and follow API usage guidelines.

Do not scrape pages aggressively.

Do not invent API endpoints or assume every field is available for every language.

Handle missing entries gracefully.

## B. Wikipedia for contextual learning

Use Wikipedia to enrich lessons with contextual information.

For example:
- A lesson about Indian festivals may link to a relevant encyclopedia article.
- A lesson about geography may provide additional cultural context.
- A lesson about a city may link to the relevant article.

Use the Wikimedia REST API or MediaWiki Action API to retrieve relevant page summaries and metadata.

Do not treat Wikipedia article titles as a complete dictionary.

Do not automatically treat the first sentence of an encyclopedia article as the definition of an ordinary word.

## C. Attribution

For reused Wikimedia content, display appropriate source attribution.

Where relevant, include:
- Entry or article title.
- Wikimedia project.
- Source page.
- Applicable license.
- Author or revision information where required and available.

Provide a dedicated Data Sources page explaining how Wikimedia content is used.

Respect the license attached to the actual source content.

Do not claim that all Wikimedia material has the same license.

Do not use Wikimedia branding in a way that suggests official endorsement.

## D. API behavior

Implement:
- Request timeouts.
- Error handling.
- Rate-limit handling.
- Appropriate caching.
- Retry logic with reasonable limits.
- Clear user-facing error messages.
- A local vocabulary fallback.

Never make the entire learning application dependent on a live Wikimedia API request succeeding.

Use an appropriate identifying User-Agent for requests when required by the selected API.

Store reusable vocabulary records locally after successful retrieval, subject to the applicable licensing requirements.

## E. Language correctness

Verify the language of each retrieved entry.

A search result in the wrong language must not silently become a vocabulary card.

When an exact English-to-Hindi, English-to-Bengali, or English-to-Marathi translation cannot be verified, display an honest unavailable-data message rather than inventing an answer.

